    "pages": [
      {
        "id": "p0",
        "title": "Momentum Wins Games",
        "text": "EFZ is a momentum game: there is no absolute guard and mixups are brutal, so the player who controls space usually controls the match. Taking ground safely - without walking into a poke - is a skill of its own."
      },
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "title": "How to Walk Forward",
        "text": "Advance in small steps BEHIND your own threat range. When the opponent pokes, either block it and keep your ground, or make it whiff and take the space it just gave up. Never walk in a straight line into an active poke."
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "title": "The Drill",
        "text": "Close the distance on Misaki step by step: walk in and block her poke, dash in to punish a miss, then use a low attack's recovery to jump forward. Each exchange should leave you closer than before."
      }
    ],
